# Round 960 — the A/B kit's own runbook was the one Round 950 counted as
# untracked and left that way. Its manifest sha256 is pinned in the R469/R470
# ledger entries, so the kit is frozen evidence the tree cites, not scratch.
!/claudedocs/phase1-ab-experiment/
/claudedocs/phase1-ab-experiment/**/*.atomic.json
/claudedocs/phase1-ab-experiment/**/*.playthrough.json
# Round 959 — the side-table runbook was authored at Round 958 and left
# untracked, so the protocol it says it FROZE existed in one working tree
# only. The exception goes in when the runbook is written, not when the arm
# runs: an untracked runbook is invisible to CI and to a fresh clone.
!/claudedocs/phase1-side-table-authoring-experiment/
/claudedocs/phase1-side-table-authoring-experiment/**/*.atomic.json
/claudedocs/phase1-side-table-authoring-experiment/**/*.playthrough.json
/claudedocs/phase1-side-table-authoring-experiment/*/run/*/contract.txt
